+# NOTE: Historically "getmodpath" performed a "replace(".[", "[")"
+        # on the module path string to normalise representations of parameter
+        # values that contained ".[" (e.g. "..[").  This early change was
+        # made to accommodate an older workspace that stored identifiers in a
+        # format where a leading dot before an opening bracket was undesirable.
+        # We discovered that this transformation corrupts real test names that
+        # legitimately contain a dot before a bracket, such as the pytest
+        # parametrize value "..[" which ends up as "test_boo[.[]" in the
+        # headline.  The correct behaviour is to preserve the original
+        # representation.  Therefore we simply return the joined path
+        # without the replace.
+        return s
 
